WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.289 --> 00:00:01.915
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.915 --> 00:00:04.088
- [Kelly] Have a seat!

00:00:04.088 --> 00:00:05.243
I love this dress.

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:06.757
- I'm so hungover.

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:07.872
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:07.872 --> 00:00:09.630
I am so hungover.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.100
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, that's the worst.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.270
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.103
- I always walk in...

00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:14.820
I love when I walk in and
Glo, my makeup artist...

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.943
I'm like, I'm sorry.

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:18.704
- My face looks drained.
- You've got a lot of work

00:00:18.704 --> 00:00:19.537
to do.

00:00:19.537 --> 00:00:20.910
- Yeah, you're gonna
earn that money today.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.743
- I need the stuff,

00:00:21.743 --> 00:00:23.190
you know, that you fill in the walls with,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.540
you call it Polyfilla here.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.310
You know, if there's a hole in the wall,

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.990
and you try and make it look better?

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.450
I need a lot of that
packed into my face today.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.650
- Yes.
- I'm feeling that.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.940
- Well, thank you for being here, that's-

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.110
- I'm here 'cause it's you.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.991
- Oh gosh, I love you.

00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:36.824
(audience cheers)

00:00:36.824 --> 00:00:39.270
Well, welcome back to the show.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.320
And it's summertime now.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.520
So what do you do for summer?

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.353
Do you go on holiday?

00:00:42.353 --> 00:00:43.186
Do you do anything fun?

00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:45.000
- Well I try to, because obviously...

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.610
I don't know when you guys
have your school holidays

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.860
but ours are like end of July

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.687
until the beginning of September, so-

00:00:51.687 --> 00:00:52.590
- Oh, it's shorter.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.940
- Yeah, ours is then.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.500
- Really glad I'm American right now.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.000
- Yes.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.770
Because that's our window of sun.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.320
We're like...
- Oh!

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.620
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.453
That's amazing.

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:04.080
I didn't think about that.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:04.913
- Where did you go?

00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:06.060
Did you ever do anything fun?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.380
Did you like family trips growing up?

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.030
- Well, yes we did actually.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.560
My mom's an opera singer

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.600
or was before she retired.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.660
So we would go on her opera tour with her.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.610
- That's incredible.
- Which is just not normal.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.570
Yeah, incredible.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.450
Yeah, the first knowledge I had of America

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.647
was like Austin and New Orleans,

00:01:23.647 --> 00:01:24.750
and San Antonio.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.770
Yeah.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.680
- Your first entrance
to America was Texas.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.060
That's awesome.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.200
- Yeah.
- It's very different.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.120
- Yeah, but also like,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.742
because she was singing, you know,

00:01:34.742 --> 00:01:37.740
the Metropolitan Opera House in New York.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.840
And so that was my first little thing,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.160
you know, obviously being a singer,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.633
I was like...
- Wow.

00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:44.010
- It's just magic, yeah.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.180
Sitting in the orchestra.
- I've been there.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.260
- So my holidays were not normal.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.150
You know, it wasn't like
just going on a beach.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.830
- Is that when you kind
of figured out like,

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.930
I wanna be a singer as well?

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:55.763
- I think so.

00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:57.120
I mean, what were you...

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.500
People asked me that and I'm like,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.300
I don't remember wanting
to do anything else.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.120
And when I heard that
people had grown up jobs,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.550
I remember thinking, "They... They what?"

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.200
- Why would you do that?
- Yeah.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.810
Why would you not just
sing, dance and act?

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.180
I honestly couldn't compute it.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.013
- I love that.

00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:13.920
What an amazing childhood.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.300
I remember going...

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.440
I'm the opposite.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.180
I was brought up where
you just had real jobs.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.920
And then I was like, "Wait,
you can make money doing that?"

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.720
You know, I was just like, "Wait, what?"

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.650
Yeah, I thought that was-

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.420
- Yeah, I think 'cause
of my mom's influence,

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.220
I don't think they were surprised

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.850
when I wanted nothing to do
with a grown-up profession.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.740
- Like a cubicle?
- Yeah.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.180
- Well our daughters
are about the same age.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.013
Does she get to travel with you?

00:02:34.013 --> 00:02:35.280
'Cause you get to travel so much.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.590
- Yes, but I'm finding now that she's...

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.930
I find it really inconvenient
that she's at school.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.940
I want her to come out and play with me.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.080
- Mine finds it inconvenient, too.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.010
She wants to go with me.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.630
- Yeah, they've got to that age

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.140
where you kind of have to respect
their education, you know?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.010
Which is a bit difficult,

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.350
but I'm gonna try and bring her a bit more

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.670
and maybe bring a tutor or something.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.880
Because coming to things
like this, for her to see...

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.700
Our girlies, seeing us working

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.260
and how important it is.
- That's an education.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.977
- Yeah, that women are just like,

00:03:02.977 --> 00:03:04.320
"I'm getting out there."

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.790
- So I agree with that too.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.230
Obviously, we love school too.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.343
- We love school.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.133
Very important.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.370
- So wait, does she know...

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.203
When you were traveling,

00:03:12.203 --> 00:03:13.170
does she know that her mom

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.979
once got kicked out of a hotel?

00:03:14.979 --> 00:03:17.340
- I don't know what you're talking about.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.173
So, look....

00:03:18.173 --> 00:03:20.361
Look, can I just say that

00:03:20.361 --> 00:03:25.020
if you're going to leave a
hostess trolley in a corridor

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.730
when people have had a
little beverage or two-

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.780
- You're inviting trouble.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.940
- Right, you are inviting trouble.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.590
So I lay on top of it,

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.750
my friend lay through it,

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.440
and another friend of ours
pushed us down the corridor,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.210
and we accidentally smacked into this...

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.043
You know, when the wheels are like

00:03:40.043 --> 00:03:41.820
(imitating wheels clacking)

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.310
Smacked into this thing and
this woman opens the door

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.437
and goes, "Well, thank you very much!

00:03:45.437 --> 00:03:47.250
I just got my baby to sleep!"

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.040
And we had to go
downstairs and sign a thing

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.293
saying we'd never come back to the hotel.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.497
- You're so cool!

00:03:54.497 --> 00:03:56.250
Here's my thing.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.840
I heard this story and I was like,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.030
that got you kicked out?
- Yes!

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.310
- Do you know what kinds
of things I have seen

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.750
and heard on tour?

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.700
Like, I can't even...

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.860
I was like, wow.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.080
A lot of people I know would've....

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.640
Would've been kicked out.
- They were not happy.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.810
And I actually thought they were...

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.850
'Cause I was there to do all my fittings

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.920
for "Spamalot" on Broadway.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.510
And I thought, "Oh, my god.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.150
They're gonna think I'm
an English reprobate."

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.650
- They'll think you're fun!

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.774
- Honestly, yeah, not good.

00:04:24.774 --> 00:04:25.980
(audience applauding)

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.820
- The season finale of "Ted
Lasso" is about to happen.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.530
And I've heard it might be the end-end.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.400
Is it the end-end?

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.270
- Well, I don't know.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:38.270
I mean, Jason says it's the
end of that three-season arc.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.140
- Oh, interesting.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.510
- Yeah, I mean, I feel like trapping him

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.360
in a dungeon with a notepad and a pen.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.193
- That's a good idea.
- And just going,

00:04:46.193 --> 00:04:48.750
"Dude, what are you doing?"

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.010
You can't step away from it.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.080
The characters are so
beloved and we all love it.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.041
I mean, I would play her when
her teeth are falling out

00:04:55.041 --> 00:04:57.690
in a retirement home sitting outside it

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.910
with mud splashing her, you know?

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.253
I just want to see her through.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.800
I love her so much.
- I love the idea that though.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.400
Of almost taking a show and
doing it in different...

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.050
Like, almost how they do with Marvel,

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:10.883
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:10.883 --> 00:05:11.716
You'd see different characters
and different things.

00:05:11.716 --> 00:05:12.990
That's a cool idea.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.113
Y'all should do that, Jason.

00:05:15.113 --> 00:05:16.980
- I know, Jason.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:17.813
Where's the camera?

00:05:17.813 --> 00:05:18.660
Jason.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.885
- I love that you do an
American for "Jason."

00:05:20.885 --> 00:05:21.718
- Jason!

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:23.821
- Okay, so on the show,

00:05:23.821 --> 00:05:26.040
Ted brings you the biscuits, right?

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:26.873
- Yes.

00:05:26.873 --> 00:05:29.280
- So, okay, you say the actual cookie

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.600
isn't actually that good right?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.433
- They weren't.

00:05:31.433 --> 00:05:34.170
Season one, they were
absolutely revolting.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.800
You know, like a ceiling
tile in a bathroom?

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.940
It was like...

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.820
Like making all your saliva disappear.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.900
But they also didn't know

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.870
that I was gonna go at
them like a crazy loon.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.331
Like (imitates devouring food).

00:05:47.331 --> 00:05:50.310
Because I wanted it to be
like her emotional support.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.720
Like a crutch.
- Emotional eating?

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.303
I don't know what you're referring to.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.380
I'm lost!

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.030
- Oh me, yeah.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.040
I've had a lot of that lately.
- So did they get better?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:05:59.873
- They did get better.
- Okay.

00:05:59.873 --> 00:06:01.650
- Do you think it's because you were like,

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.797
these are (beep)?
- Jason was like,

00:06:02.797 --> 00:06:04.410
"God, I don't know why they've got better

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.897
when you've complained
about them globally."

00:06:06.897 --> 00:06:08.190
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.023
- I don't know what's happening there.

00:06:09.023 --> 00:06:09.856
- But do you know what?
- There's a link.

00:06:09.856 --> 00:06:12.420
- If you add a lot of
butter and a lot of sugar,

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.740
you could be eating an old shoe

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.480
and it would taste nice.
- Absolutely.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.243
- Just pile on all the lard and the sugar.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.980
- The lard.
- No, they're good.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.940
They're good now.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.290
- So the show inspired

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.060
a new ice cream flavor at Jeni's.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:24.902
It's called "Biscuits with the Boss."

00:06:24.902 --> 00:06:26.100
- I haven't tried it yet.
- You haven't?

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.890
Okay, we didn't know if you
tried it, so we have some.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:29.723
I'm gonna try it with you.

00:06:29.723 --> 00:06:32.181
I've never tried it either.
- Ooh, ooh!

00:06:32.181 --> 00:06:33.570
- It might need more sugar.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.517
- We just need to be watching a movie.

00:06:35.517 --> 00:06:36.810
Get some chips and dips.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.400
- I'm down, I'm down.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.260
- Oh my god, I love this.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.093
Look at the packaging.

00:06:41.093 --> 00:06:43.620
- Wait, look at your fancy wooden fork.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.810
Only the best at "The
Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.797
- Fancy.
- Okay, I'm tasting it.

00:06:46.797 --> 00:06:48.690
- [Hannah] Oh, look, there's
a biscuit box on the...

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.531
Oh, my gosh.
- Okay.

00:06:50.531 --> 00:06:51.870
- [Hannah] Oh, this is perfect timing.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.790
- You know you've made it
when they make a flavor,

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.620
is all I'm saying.
- Oh, my god.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.537
This is literally gonna
do my hangover a treat.

00:06:59.537 --> 00:07:00.660
(audience laughs)

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.493
- [Kelly] Or you'll have an encore later.

00:07:02.493 --> 00:07:04.544
- That is so much nicer.
- Than the...

00:07:04.544 --> 00:07:05.571
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:05.571 --> 00:07:07.380
- [Hannah] That's so much nicer.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.480
- It's interesting 'cause
it's got the biscuit flavor.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.700
I dug in to make sure I had it all.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.533
That's good!

00:07:12.533 --> 00:07:13.366
- Look!

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.550
Big dirty chunks!

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.600
- Yes, it's very shortbread-y.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.517
- Ooh!

00:07:17.517 --> 00:07:18.570
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:19.920
- It's very shortbread-y.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:20.790
I like it.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.020
- I'm just gonna keep going.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.400
- Go ahead.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.050
I'm just warning you after a hangover,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.776
it might not end well, but anyway...

00:07:26.776 --> 00:07:27.609
(Hannah laughs)

00:07:27.609 --> 00:07:29.160
- It might come back.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:32.280
You just co-hosted one of
my favorite shows actually.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.570
I love Eurovision.
- Eurovision!

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.499
- Eurovision 2023.
- Oh, my god.

00:07:35.499 --> 00:07:36.332
- [Kelly] How was it?

00:07:36.332 --> 00:07:37.165
How is it being a part of that show?

00:07:37.165 --> 00:07:39.060
- [Hannah] Honestly, just insane.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.020
- [Kelly] You grew up on it?

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.310
- Yeah, I totally grew up on it.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.050
I'm from musical theater, for God's sake.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.490
- Because I love Eurovision too,

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.078
with Will Ferrell and Rachel.

00:07:46.078 --> 00:07:47.580
- But they got that spot-on.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:48.413
- [Kelly] Yeah, I know!

00:07:48.413 --> 00:07:49.890
But that's why I loved it.
- Yeah.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.930
But there's been some amazing guys

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.725
that have come out of that.
- Måneskin!

00:07:53.725 --> 00:07:54.960
- Måneskin.
- I love Måneskin.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.010
- Oh my god, I love them.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.440
And then back in the
day we had Bucks Fizz.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.270
I mean, which would never happen now.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.870
Like, a four-people group and two girls.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.130
And in one part of the song,

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.750
the guys whip the girls' skirts off

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.890
and they've got like minis.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:10.417
And I was like, can you
imagine a woman going,

00:08:10.417 --> 00:08:11.430
"Oh no, that's cool."

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:12.960
Now?
- "Yeah, let's do it."

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:13.980
- Oh, my god.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:16.260
- I know, but I think
that's what's so funny,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.790
Not funny, but just entertaining

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.665
is like, how outrageous it can get.

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.498
- [Hannah] That's the best part of it.

00:08:20.498 --> 00:08:22.020
- Even like Måneskin,

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.850
they're outrageous in
the way that they look.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.760
They're, first of all, in
a Vogue shoot all the time.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.280
It's very theatrical,
but like, their attire,

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.301
their aesthetic is cool
and the songs are rad.

00:08:31.301 --> 00:08:32.134
- Yeah.

00:08:32.134 --> 00:08:33.870
- I mean obviously like ABBA, Celine Dion,

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:34.980
there's so many winners from that show

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.780
that went on to be musicians.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.310
- I mean, Celine Dion.
- Yeah.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.410
- God, what we would've given

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.930
to hear her sing back then with that.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.550
I mean, just incredible.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.870
Yeah, so it's been quite overwhelming.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:46.980
But I'd never worked

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.830
with an in-ear doo-da.
- I hate it.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.420
I am not the person for that.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.253
- You know what's I do?

00:08:52.253 --> 00:08:53.250
This....

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.083
- Yeah, you go like...

00:08:54.083 --> 00:08:55.650
- I look up and I'm just like...

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.240
I hate... I literally begged-

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.125
- It's like trying
figure out who's farted.

00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:02.613
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:02.613 --> 00:09:03.570
It's not good.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.620
- It's not good for me either.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:05.820
I don't do well.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.380
- I have to stop myself going,

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.067
sorry, 180 million people.

00:09:09.067 --> 00:09:10.444
"What?"

00:09:10.444 --> 00:09:11.277
Awful.

00:09:11.277 --> 00:09:13.350
- Yeah, I didn't get used to it.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:14.183
I didn't at all.

00:09:14.183 --> 00:09:15.510
And then the crowd gets
so loud and you're like...

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.077
It almost sounds like
Charlie Brown's teacher,

00:09:17.077 --> 00:09:18.300
"Wah, wah, wah, wah."

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.857
And you're like, I don't
understand what you're saying.

00:09:19.857 --> 00:09:21.630
And we're on live television.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.580
Anyway, it was a hit.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:24.420
Okay, so I don't know about you

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.700
but I am terrible at words,
like remembering words.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:27.870
- Rubbish.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.687
- And I write them, but
I still forget them.

00:09:30.687 --> 00:09:31.800
- You write them but you still forget.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.583
- Literally, the songs I write, I forget.

00:09:33.583 --> 00:09:36.147
- You forget your own words?
- All the time.

00:09:36.147 --> 00:09:37.860
- Oh my god, I love this.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.630
- Yeah, I can literally...

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.463
It's a talent.

00:09:40.463 --> 00:09:42.480
I can be staring at the words

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.280
and still sing something different.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.810
I don't know what that means.
- Do you know what that is?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:46.800
Motherhood.
- Yeah.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.630
And I'm ADHD, so I'm also...

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.856
My brain is just always
thinking of a thousand things.

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.890
- I'm a little bit like, "Squirrel!"

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.110
- Oh, that's literally
what I say, is squirrel.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.102
Okay, so we're so much alike.

00:09:57.102 --> 00:09:59.910
So should we play a game
to find out who is worse?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.342
- Yes, let's see how bad I am in a game.

00:10:02.342 --> 00:10:03.175
Let's do it.

00:10:03.175 --> 00:10:04.008
- Yes, let's do it.

00:10:04.008 --> 00:10:05.580
We're gonna go to a break.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.950
The finale of "Ted
Lasso" is tomorrow night

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.213
on Apple TV Plus.

